# s8_encrypt_on_convert (off-path)
#
# basis      s7_graph_clear_values peak 2061808 kB; single pool (host):
#   heap:_multiarray_umath...+0x13ab14   865.8 MB   0.410 of the peak   <- this step
#   heap:libc10.so+0x4a675               535.3 MB   0.254
#   anon:[heap]                          269.9 MB   0.128               allocator arena, never a target
#
# object     plaintext weights held twice (probe_convert_trace_cpu.py, steps/s7_graph_clear_values/evidence/):
#   CONVERT|before_parse            RSS 1102628  torch_bytes=433258512
#   CONVERT|initializer_0_of_201    RSS 1283976  torch_bytes=522334224
#   CONVERT|initializer_200_of_201  RSS 1610724  torch_bytes=866505752
#            torch.from_numpy(numpy_helper.to_array(node)) (nn/onnx_converter.py:183) while the HF model
#            lives: 2 x 433.25 MB (duplication).
# fix        1. caller's model released before the parse (plaintext_free_early_cpu)
#            2. each initializer encrypted in its creating loop (encrypt_on_convert_cpu)
#            part 1 alone: -1284 kB = -0.06% vs 1.364% spread (off-path/s8_plaintext_free_early/).
# draws      Module.encrypt per initializer = set_parameter(name, crypten.cryptensor(param, src=src,
#            requires_grad=...)) (nn/module.py:482-490), same calls, tensors and order. The later
#            private_model.encrypt() finds nothing to convert (Parameter.__init__ :1126; skip at :478).
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: _multiarray_umath.cpython-310-x86_64-linux-gnu.so+0x13ab14
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_early_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,beaver_reveal_inplace_cpu,graph_clear_values_cpu,param_mmap_release_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,encrypt_on_convert_cpu
